From 4c4cb5c821ada4a8f92268a677ae35aa77f4a447 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:58:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AudioEngine/VideoPlayer: the downmix settings that Kodi lacks

For whoever plays 5.1 or 7.1 on a TV, a stereo sound bar or headphones.
Kodi has, for a downmix, the centre level of each video (its audio
settings, -10 to +30 dB in steps of 1 dB, kept in the library as a whole
number), "Include LFE when downmixing" (Off, 50 % or 100 %) and "Maintain
original volume on downmix". It takes the centre level that the track asks
for (FFmpeg's AV_FRAME_DATA_DOWNMIX_INFO: AC-3's cmixlev, E-AC-3's) and adds
the video's to it. What it lacks, now in Settings > System > Audio, with
those (ideas of pannal's CoreELEC builds, p3i):

- "Centre channel level when downmixing" (audiooutput.hadescentrelevel):
  -10 to +10 dB in steps of 0.5 dB, 0.0 by default, added to the track's
  level and to the video's. The library's column stays as it is (a library
  shared with other Kodi systems keeps a whole number there).
- "Use the track's centre level when downmixing"
  (audiooutput.hadesdownmixlevels), on by default: off, the centre is mixed
  at -3 dB, as for a track that asks for none.
- "Include LFE when downmixing" takes 150 %, 200 % and 300 % too (Kodi's
  own setting; swresample's lfe_mix_level, which puts it into the front
  left and right of a stereo downmix, or the centre where there is one).

The centre level is DownmixLevels.h's, read for every frame as before:
they apply at once. kodi.log says the level when a Hades setting changes
it. The engine's resampler uses it only where it downmixes: sound that is
passed through, or that plays on as many speakers as it has, does not
change.

Tested on the host with Kodi's own mixer (CActiveAEResampleFFMPEG, with
AEUtil.cpp and AEChannelInfo.cpp, over FFmpeg 9.0.2's libswresample;
downmix_test.cpp): with the defaults, the centre level is Kodi's
expression bit for bit for every level of the video and every centre level
a track can ask for (328 cases), and the mix is Kodi's bit for bit; the
matrices of 5.1 and 7.1 into stereo, with and without "Maintain original
volume", are the ones expected for each setting and LFE level; 5.1 on 5.1
and 7.1 on 7.1 with every setting at its far end are passed as they are,
bit for bit.
